    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73cb36b2_af48f74d",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530208
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-28T18:27:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like all heaps that are not standard heaps, must be of type custom. Otherwise, it will be considered invalid in the ion.c code when the heap is registered. However, doesn\u0027t this make this restrictive for vendors? All of their heaps will be of type custom, so if they need to distinguish between different types of custom heaps, they can\u0027t really do that?\n\nI guess it doesn\u0027t really make sense for anyone to use \"ION_HEAP_TYPE_CUSTOM\" as a type, as I would imagine vendors want a finer granule for heap type classification. So, is the purpose of this just to serve as a boundary marker? If so, then the ion.c code needs to be modified.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "93a8029497b5344a47d0a9b868ecd6984ec21804",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc956d51_f05b9a48",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1108565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-28T20:49:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e so if they need to distinguish between different types of custom heaps, they can\u0027t really do that?\nNot sure why would you want to have a different type for different heaps, since the type is pretty much a useless and isn\u0027t what is used to identify heaps to allocate from (heap ids are).\n\nThe only possible reason I can think of is may be it makes debugging easier. I don\u0027t have a strong opinion about this though, so I\u0027ll make the ion.c code change to allow heap types to be [ION_HEAP_TYPE_CUSTOM - 32). I guess in that case, I do need a max heap type, which I am going to make 31 now as an arbitrary choice.",
      "parentUuid": "73cb36b2_af48f74d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "93a8029497b5344a47d0a9b868ecd6984ec21804",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
